description:
FOUND (s526w1, YAML-Tiny census: t/20_subclass.t, t/21_yamlpm_compat.t, t/12_write.t die "Undefined subroutine &YAML::Tiny::refaddr called"; YAML/Tiny.pm 692/731 call refaddr(...), 833 `*refaddr = *Scalar::Util::refaddr;` in a BEGIN, 854 `delete $YAML::Tiny::{refaddr};`).
Probe (scratch p-stdel.pl):
  package P;
  sub use_it { return helper(5) }
  BEGIN { *helper = sub { "h$_[0]" } }
  sub plain { "p" } sub use_plain { plain() }
  delete $P::{helper}; delete $P::{plain};
  package main;
  print P::use_it(), " ", P::use_plain(), " ", (defined &{"P::helper"} ? "def" : "undef"), "\n";
perl 5.40.3: "h5 p undef".  PCL: dies "Undefined subroutine &P::helper called".
The stash-delete half (#3511) removes the sub; perl's compiled call sites keep the CV (the same pinned-glob rule #3691 applies to a non-sub symbol: compiled references keep their cell).  Related: #3696 (the opposite direction: `defined &name` compiled AFTER the delete).  Rows: YAML-Tiny 20_subclass *FILE*, 21_yamlpm_compat *FILE*, 12_write *PLAN* + 1 (write ascii characters) and whatever writes in the tml files.  Layer: compiler/runtime name binding.
